WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.165 --> 00:00:01.860
- [barista] Coffee be
ready just over there.

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.187
- [customer] Thanks, man.

00:00:03.187 --> 00:00:03.687
- [barista] Hey, bud.

00:00:03.687 --> 00:00:04.420
What can I get for ya'?

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:05.935
- Uh, can I get a medium coffee to go?

00:00:05.935 --> 00:00:07.354
- Medium coffee, got it.

00:00:07.354 --> 00:00:08.004
Name?

00:00:08.004 --> 00:00:08.603
- Zack.

00:00:08.603 --> 00:00:12.703
- Zack, (shooting sounds) Zack Attack.

00:00:12.703 --> 00:00:13.534
- Um...

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:15.468
- Hey Justin, can I get a medium brew

00:00:15.468 --> 00:00:17.936
for my main bro, Zack Attack?

00:00:17.936 --> 00:00:18.553
- [Justin] Zack Attack?

00:00:18.553 --> 00:00:19.386
- Zack Attack!

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:20.120
- I like that.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.553
- Right? Zack Attack.

00:00:21.553 --> 00:00:22.293
- Zack Attack.

00:00:22.462 --> 00:00:23.878
- Zack Attack.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.019
- Zack Attack!

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:26.921
- (drumming noises) Zack Attack.

00:00:26.921 --> 00:00:28.184
- Hello, Mr. President?

00:00:28.184 --> 00:00:30.264
Yeah, uh, the world is
under a Zack Attack.

00:00:30.264 --> 00:00:35.109
- Whoa, Justin, (panting)
I'm having a Zack Attack.

00:00:35.109 --> 00:00:36.554
Hey everybody? Attention please!

00:00:36.554 --> 00:00:38.581
Put your coffees down, laptops closed.

00:00:38.581 --> 00:00:40.831
Let's give it up for my
main man, Zack Attack!

00:00:40.831 --> 00:00:43.563
- No, you don't have to
do, oh, c'mon, no, oh...

00:00:43.563 --> 00:00:48.415
- [everybody] Zack Attack,
Zack Attack, Zack Attack...

00:00:54.518 --> 00:00:55.273
- It was torture.

00:00:55.273 --> 00:00:57.674
I mean they all started
chanting Zack Attack.

00:00:57.674 --> 00:00:59.698
It made me feel like a
frickin' six-year-old.

00:00:59.698 --> 00:01:02.356
- Yeah, the life of a white
straight male is so hard.

00:01:02.356 --> 00:01:03.937
- I actually don't think
it's that bad of a nickname.

00:01:03.937 --> 00:01:04.746
- Look, you guys don't get it.

00:01:04.746 --> 00:01:06.714
You all have amazing nicknames.

00:01:06.714 --> 00:01:07.714
Sara Bear.

00:01:07.714 --> 00:01:09.013
Neal's on Wheels.

00:01:09.013 --> 00:01:10.607
Yo Gabby Gabby.

00:01:10.607 --> 00:01:12.030
I just want to be called Zack.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.013
Just plain Zack, is that
too much to ask for?

00:01:14.013 --> 00:01:14.964
- What up, Zack Attack?

00:01:14.964 --> 00:01:15.664
- God damn it!

00:01:15.664 --> 00:01:16.680
Okay, you know what?

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:17.846
First thing tomorrow,
I'm gonna go in there,

00:01:17.846 --> 00:01:19.582
and I'm gonna tell the
barista what's what.

00:01:19.582 --> 00:01:22.807
No one is ever gonna call
me Zack Attack ever again.

00:01:22.807 --> 00:01:25.497
- Honey, that is so sweet of you.

00:01:25.497 --> 00:01:26.196
- Thank you!

00:01:26.196 --> 00:01:27.581
I mean, just think about it, okay?

00:01:27.581 --> 00:01:30.680
Some lonely tech worker, same
routine every single morning.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:33.096
He goes to work, he works,
he punches in, punches out,

00:01:33.096 --> 00:01:34.263
but then... (claps)

00:01:34.263 --> 00:01:34.997
- Zack Attack!

00:01:34.997 --> 00:01:37.396
- Yes! Zack Attack, yes, Abby!

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:39.381
- I bet you blew his mind!

00:01:39.381 --> 00:01:41.997
- Oh no, I shook it up a little bit,

00:01:41.997 --> 00:01:43.346
added some color into his life.

00:01:43.346 --> 00:01:45.747
- Sent him straight back to childhood.

00:01:45.747 --> 00:01:46.880
- You know what I did?

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:48.796
I gave him his fight club.

00:01:48.796 --> 00:01:50.646
- You're so fucking hot right now.

00:01:50.646 --> 00:01:52.513
- No, you are.

00:01:52.821 --> 00:01:54.530
- Do you think you'll see him tomorrow?

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:57.013
- Maybe, but, maybe not.

00:01:57.013 --> 00:01:59.131
- Hey, who wouldn't want
to get Zack Attacked again?

00:01:59.131 --> 00:02:00.513
- Oh, he will.

00:02:00.513 --> 00:02:01.813
Don't worry, he will.

00:02:01.813 --> 00:02:03.030
- What do you mean?

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.247
- Well, you know how sometimes I stay late

00:02:04.247 --> 00:02:05.453
to use the work computer?

00:02:05.453 --> 00:02:06.187
- Uh huh.

00:02:06.187 --> 00:02:08.585
- I knew that just one Zack
Attack wasn't gonna be enough

00:02:08.585 --> 00:02:11.478
to change Zack's boring life around, so

00:02:11.478 --> 00:02:13.802
I hacked into the California
Government database,

00:02:13.802 --> 00:02:16.980
and I legally changed
his name to Zack Attack!

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.846
- Like on his driver's license and stuff?

00:02:18.846 --> 00:02:21.364
- Yeah, birth certificate,
tax identification,

00:02:21.364 --> 00:02:22.736
even all the federal stuff.

00:02:22.736 --> 00:02:25.164
- Ah, babe, he's gonna love that!

00:02:25.164 --> 00:02:26.646
- So that's not even the end of it.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.331
So, I did a little more hacking,

00:02:28.331 --> 00:02:30.464
and I realized that reality itself

00:02:30.464 --> 00:02:33.160
is just a simulation that's run entirely

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:35.063
out of the coffee shop back room computer!

00:02:35.063 --> 00:02:36.998
- [Abby] Consciousness is
just a stream of electrons

00:02:36.998 --> 00:02:39.563
that exists in a computer
in a virtual coffee shop?

00:02:39.563 --> 00:02:40.797
- Yes, Abby, yes!

00:02:40.797 --> 00:02:41.831
Everything is!

00:02:41.831 --> 00:02:43.122
The feeling of the sun's warmth

00:02:43.122 --> 00:02:44.680
as it rains across your face.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.714
- The joy of holding your newborn child!

00:02:46.714 --> 00:02:48.298
- All just binary bits of information

00:02:48.298 --> 00:02:49.847
being processed on what I assume to be

00:02:49.847 --> 00:02:51.946
is an inter-dimensional quantum computer!

00:02:51.946 --> 00:02:53.430
- That's pretty cool!

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.881
- I had access to alter
anything in our world.

00:02:55.881 --> 00:02:56.914
- [Abby] You could cure cancer!

00:02:56.914 --> 00:02:57.395
- Yes!

00:02:57.395 --> 00:02:58.464
- You could end world hunger!

00:02:58.464 --> 00:02:58.930
- Yes!

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.346
- You could resurrect lost loved ones!

00:03:01.346 --> 00:03:05.381
- I had the power to end
human suffering forever!

00:03:05.381 --> 00:03:07.131
- So what did you do?

00:03:07.131 --> 00:03:09.582
- I did the only logical thing

00:03:09.582 --> 00:03:11.964
a man in my position could do.

00:03:11.964 --> 00:03:16.207
I changed every instance of
Zack's name to Zack Attack

00:03:16.207 --> 00:03:18.313
in this universe and
every alternate universe

00:03:18.313 --> 00:03:20.513
past, present, and future.

00:03:20.513 --> 00:03:21.870
- Wow.

00:03:22.086 --> 00:03:23.872
That is so selfless.

00:03:23.872 --> 00:03:24.905
- I know.

00:03:24.905 --> 00:03:27.214
- Do you think it changed anything else?

00:03:27.214 --> 00:03:28.363
- And can I get your name?

00:03:28.363 --> 00:03:29.863
- Uh, yeah, it's Zack Attack.

00:03:29.863 --> 00:03:30.997
- Got it, Zack.

00:03:30.997 --> 00:03:33.896
- No, no, Zack Attack.

00:03:33.896 --> 00:03:36.294
There's an Attack at the end, not Zack.

00:03:36.294 --> 00:03:37.464
- Oh, okay.

00:03:37.464 --> 00:03:38.747
- Oh, Hitler, hey, what's up, man?

00:03:38.747 --> 00:03:41.094
- Oh, Zack Attack, what is up?

00:03:41.094 --> 00:03:43.831
One cappuccino, please, Fraulein.

00:03:44.492 --> 00:03:45.665
- [barista] And can I get a name for that?

00:03:45.665 --> 00:03:46.964
- Uh, Hitler.

00:03:46.964 --> 00:03:47.757
- [barista] Alright, Heather.

00:03:47.757 --> 00:03:48.548
That'll be out in a few minutes.

00:03:48.548 --> 00:03:51.529
- Uh, this always happens, it's Hitler.

00:03:51.529 --> 00:03:55.180
So that's an H - I - T - L - E - R,

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.596
there's no Heather, there's only one H.

00:03:57.596 --> 00:03:59.606
- Zack Attack!

